WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.421
This slide focuses on Running totals are a core
analytics pattern The goal is to

00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:12.073
understand the idea in plain language before
connecting it to code or analytical use Loop

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.402
+ accumulator An accumulator is a variable that
starts with a simple value then updates

00:00:17.415 --> 00:00:24.333
during each loop repetition Accumulate a total
inside a loop Before

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.533
running the example predict what the output should
look like Run it in the browser

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:35.533
inspect the result then change one value condition
or input and run it again Pay

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:41.285
attention to what changed and why This pattern
appears often in summaries

00:00:41.311 --> 00:00:46.893
and reports The total begins at 0 Each amount is
added to

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:48.077
the previous total
